[5] Flow/cut theorem target
  Residual capacitor lemma:
    In any automatic/residue fiber after status is protected, a mixed open
    route pair is a two-plate capacitor.  The first nonzero cut among exact
    scale, coarse topology, closed-arc topology, safe-component stalk,
    fusion sidecar, and packet labels must either classify the pair as
    owner_strip, nested_refinement, cross_handoff, or named residual debt.
  Current four-packet audit:
    M_q_petal_covering_capacitor exits by nested_refinement.
    boundary_topology_k33_covering_capacitor exits by cross_handoff.
  New angle:
    Treat the proof ladder as max-flow/min-cut on residual debt.  Status
    gates remove boundary/open capacity; route capacitors are then finite
    cut obligations, not new counterexample families.
